## 2. Target Architecture

### 2.1 Two coordinated packages, one source of truth

```
AgentFoundation/src/agent_foundation/ui/
│
├── (Python layer — agent_foundation.ui)
│   ├── widget_protocol.py            ← contract: WIDGET_TYPES (12 constants)
│   ├── input_modes.py                ← contract: InputMode + ChoiceOption
│   ├── interactive_base.py           ← sync + async (aget_input/asend_response)
│   ├── rich_interactive_base.py      ← supports_widgets + pending_input_mode
│   ├── terminal_interactive.py       ← webaxon lazy + optional
│   ├── queue_interactive.py          ← + asyncio.Queue + turn_boundary + token batches
│   ├── web_interactive.py            ← NEW (ported from RE, decoupled)
│   ├── interactive_checkpoint.py     ← unchanged; async bug auto-fixed
│   ├── __init__.py                   ← NEW public barrel
│   └── (graph_*, dash_interactive/ — untouched, out of scope)
│
├── widgets/                          ← NEW publishable React package
│   ├── package.json                  ← "@agent-foundation/ui-react", MUI >=5 <8
│   ├── tsup.config.ts                ← builds CJS+ESM, no consumer config needed
│   ├── README.md
│   ├── CONTRIBUTING.md               ← rules to prevent re-divergence
│   ├── scripts/
│   │   └── sync_widget_types.py      ← py → js codegen + --check mode
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── index.js                  ← public barrel
│   │   ├── protocol/
│   │   │   ├── widgetTypes.js        ← GENERATED — do not edit
│   │   │   ├── inputModeTypes.js     ← GENERATED — do not edit
│   │   │   ├── WidgetRegistry.js     ← getWidget + registerWidget (NEW)
│   │   │   ├── ChatWidgetRenderer.js
│   │   │   ├── ConversationToolWidget.js  ← input_mode dispatcher, parser prop
│   │   │   └── registerBuiltins.js   ← auto-loaded
│   │   ├── inputs/                   ← one file per widget_type
│   │   ├── common/                   ← pure primitives (no domain coupling)
│   │   ├── chat/                     ← chat/streaming primitives
│   │   ├── layout/                   ← generic chrome
│   │   ├── progress/                 ← progress UI primitives
│   │   ├── graph/                    ← agent-reasoning viz (GraphFlowView, NodeDetailPanel)
│   │   ├── theme/                    ← MUI-version-agnostic theme system
│   │   │   └── themes/{dark,atlassian,pinterest}.js
│   │   └── hooks/                    ← generic hooks; messageAdapter prop on WS hooks
│   ├── tests/                        ← Vitest + RTL snapshot tests
│   └── stories/                      ← Storybook (deferred to v0.2.0 if needed)
│
└── webui/                            ← demo / reference app (NOT the library)
    ├── react/                        ← consumes ../widgets via file:
    └── backend/                      ← Flask demo backend
```

**Naming decisions:**
- Package name: `@agent-foundation/ui-react` (cryptic-clock's choice; matches the
  shorter convention).
- Directory name: `ui/widgets/` (cryptic-clock's choice; resolves v3.0's
  disagreement explicitly).
- Note: the directory holds more than widgets (theme, hooks, layout). This is
  documented in `widgets/README.md` opening sentence and in CONTRIBUTING.md.

### 2.2 Three stable contracts

The library exposes three contracts. The Python `widget_protocol.py` constants
are the source of truth; the JS side is **generated**, not hand-typed.

**Contract 1 — Wire format.** Mirrors `widget_protocol.WidgetMessage.to_dict()`:

```ts
type WidgetType =
  | 'text_input' | 'free_text'
  | 'single_choice' | 'multiple_choice' | 'multiple_choices'   // plural alias
  | 'dropdown' | 'toggle' | 'confirmation'
  | 'tool_argument_form' | 'multi_input' | 'grouped'
  | 'approval' | 'card_choice' | 'default';

type WidgetMessage = {
  widget_id: string;
  widget_type: WidgetType;
  title?: string;
  description?: string;
  input_mode?: InputModeConfigDict;
  fields?: WidgetFieldDict[];
  metadata?: Record<string, unknown>;
};

type WidgetResponse = {
  widget_id: string;
  values: Record<string, unknown>;
  action: 'submit' | 'cancel' | 'skip';
};
```

**Contract 2 — Component prop shape.** Every input widget accepts exactly:

```ts
type WidgetProps = {
  widget: WidgetMessage;            // immutable
  onSubmit: (r: WidgetResponse) => void;
  onCancel?: () => void;
  onView?: (path: string) => void;
  onViewFolder?: (path: string) => void;
  disabled?: boolean;
};
```

Legacy `{ config, data, pendingInput }` shape is supported via a
`legacyAdapter.js` shim during Phase 2 → Phase 3, removed at `0.2.0`.

**Contract 3 — Open registry.**

```js
import { registerWidget, getWidget, listRegisteredWidgets }
  from '@agent-foundation/ui-react';

// Built-in (auto-registered):
getWidget('text_input');             // → TextInputWidget

// Domain (app-side):
registerWidget('openteam.sprint_progress', SprintProgressWidget);
registerWidget('rankevolve.proposal_selection', ProposalSelectionWidget);
```

Naming convention: built-ins are **bare** strings (matching Python constants);
domain widgets MUST use **`namespace.type`**. The registry warns on
non-namespaced registration of a non-canonical type.

### 2.3 Consumption model

| Consumer | Dev loop | CI / production |
|----------|----------|-----------------|
| AF `webui/react/` (same repo) | `"@agent-foundation/ui-react": "file:../../widgets"` | Same. |
| OS `openteam/ui/` | `"@agent-foundation/ui-react": "file:../../../../AgentFoundation/src/agent_foundation/ui/widgets"` (works when both repos are checked out as siblings under `CoreProjects/`) | Same `file:` path, but only if CI checks out both repos in the same workspace layout. Otherwise: pinned npm tarball from Artifactory. |
| RE `webui/react/` (in `atlassian-packages/`) | `"@agent-foundation/ui-react": "file:../../../../../AgentFoundation/src/agent_foundation/ui/widgets"` (**5 `..`s**, not 4 — verified) | **Pinned npm tarball from Artifactory.** RE's CI runs from `atlassian-packages/` without AF checked out. |

**CRA transpilation:** because the library ships **pre-built CJS+ESM via `tsup`**,
consumers do **not** need `craco`. Plain `react-scripts start` works.
Documented as fallback: any consumer that wants to source-link can add a
15-line `craco.config.js`. v2.0's analysis of why pre-build wins is preserved
verbatim in this file's §11 (Risks).

### 2.4 Python ↔ JS sync

Single invariant: widget-type strings, `InputMode` enum values, and
`ChoiceOption` field names match exactly across languages.

```
widgets/scripts/sync_widget_types.py
  reads:  ../../widget_protocol.py, ../../input_modes.py
  writes: widgets/src/protocol/widgetTypes.js
          widgets/src/protocol/inputModeTypes.js
```

Generated files carry a banner:
`// AUTOGENERATED — DO NOT EDIT. Run scripts/sync_widget_types.py.`
CI runs `--check` and fails on drift.

